# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
production/.env

# ── Session / agent working files (not part of the app) ───────────────────────
.claude/
monitoring/

# ── Generated pipeline output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scraped/cleaned/Shopify CSVs and run logs are regenerated by every pipeline
# run and are not a source of truth. Tracking them added ~150 MB per run to the
# repo. Only the .csv/.log artifacts are ignored — the small .json caches under
# Data/ are deliberately NOT, see below.
pipelines/*/Data/**/*.csv
pipelines/*/Data/**/*.log
# Backups a backfill leaves beside the file it patched — same content class as
# the .csv above, and a .bak does not match the .csv rule.
pipelines/*/Data/**/*.bak
pipelines/*/logs/
# run_all.py opens a log handler at import time, so even a test collection
# creates this one — a directory up from the per-supplier logs/ above.
pipelines/logs/
# run_all.py invoked from the repo ROOT writes here instead of the two above.
# Same class of artifact; every file it had left behind was zero bytes.
/logs/
pipelines/dashboard_logs/
upload_ready/

# Runtime state written by the dashboard on every run (pid/status/timestamps),
# plus the enrichment scan/result snapshots — all recomputed from the CSVs and
# the cache on demand, so there is nothing here worth version-controlling.
pipelines/.dashboard_status.json
pipelines/.enrich_scan.json
pipelines/.enrich_result.json

# NOTE — intentionally still tracked:
#   pipelines/*/Data/**/*.json
# That covers serp_cache.json, which holds SerpAPI results the client has
# already PAID for. Losing it means re-buying those searches. It stays in
# version control on purpose. Same for the zero_terms_*.json scrape caches
# and the shared sku/handle maps.
#
# image_quality_cache.json belongs to the same class for a different reason:
# nothing was paid for it, but it is 3,615 image downloads, and a scan that
# has to rebuild it reports near-zero image gaps until it finishes.

# Pause/resume state of a run in progress (shared/scrape_journal.py): progress
# journals, the step reached and the PAUSE flag. Machine-local and short-lived;
# the .json in here must not fall under the tracked-cache rule above.
pipelines/*/Data/run_state/

# Quarantined no-cost-price rows are regenerated every run (data, not source)
no price detected/*.csv

# ── Coverage checks ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dated dev-store-vs-supplier reports plus the tooling that produces them. Same
# class as monitoring/: run output and analysis, regenerated on demand from the
# store and the raw scrapes, not part of the app the client runs.
coverage/

# Supplier session cookies written by refresh_cookies.py (shared/cookie_store.py).
# Short-lived and per-machine; the scrapers fall back to their own literals.
pipelines/shared/Data/session_cookies.json*

# Mac app build output (macapp/build.py).
macapp/build/
macapp/dist/
